          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+2-algebra"} Lie 2-algebra
            the
            %strong
              2-groupoid of
              = succeed "-valued" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔤
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-groupoid"} 2-groupoid
            whose objects are
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformation"} gauge transformation
            %em higher order gauge transformations
            of those.
          %p
            This naturally refines to a non-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+sheaf"} concrete
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+2-groupoid"} Lie 2-groupoid
            is the 2-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truncated"} truncated
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+groupoid"} ∞-Lie groupoid
            whose
            = succeed "-parameterized" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+2-algebra"} Lie 2-algebra
          %p
            This is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category
            generalization of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+of+Lie-algebra+valued+forms"} groupoid of Lie-algebra valued forms
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
            with coefficients in this 2-groupoid is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+2-bundle"} connection on a 2-bundle
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#for_strict_lie_2algebras For strict Lie 2-algebras
          %p
            Consider a Lie
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-group"} strict 2-group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            corresponding to a Lie
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+module"} crossed module
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 2
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi δ
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (G_2 \stackrel{\delta}{\to} G_1)
            with action
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha : G_1 \to Aut(G_2)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            for the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            2-groupoid, the one coming from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+complex"} crossed complex
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 2
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi δ
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 1
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo →
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [\mathbf{B}G]
                  \=
                  (G_2 \stackrel{\delta}{\to} G_1 \stackrel{\to}{\to} *)
                  \\,.
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mn 2
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi δ
                        %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathfrak{g}_2 \stackrel{\delta_*}{\to} \mathfrak{g}_1]
            for the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+crossed+module"} differential crossed module
            with action
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi α
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi der
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha_* : \mathfrak{g}_1 \to der(\mathfrak{g}_2)
          .un_def
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p The 2-groupoid of Lie 2-algebra valued forms is defined to be the 2-stack
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mi G
                    %mo :
                    %mi CartSp
                    %msup
                      %mrow
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mn 2
                    %mi Grpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\bar \mathbf{B}G : CartSp{}^{op} \to 2Grpd
            %p
              which assigns to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi CartSp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in CartSp
              the following 2-groupoid:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  An
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
                  is a pair
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔤
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi B
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔤
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        A \in \Omega^1(U,\mathfrak{g}_1)\,, \;\;\;
                        B \in \Omega^2(U,\mathfrak{g}_2)
                        \\,.
              %li
                %p
                  A 1-
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi g
                        %mo ,
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo :
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo ′
                        %mo ,
                        %mi B
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (g,a) : (A,B) \to (A',B')
                  is a pair
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mn ∞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi a
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔤
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        g \in C^\infty(U,G_1)\,,\;\;\; a \in \Omega^1(U,\mathfrak{g}_2)
                %p such that
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ′
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi Ad
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi g
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mn 1
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %mi A
                          %mo +
                          %msub
                            %mi δ
                            %mo *
                          %mi a
                          %mo )
                        %mo +
                        %msup
                          %mi g
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mi d
                        %mi g
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        A' = Ad_{g^{-1}}\left( A + \delta_* a \right) + g^{-1} d g
                %p and
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                        %mo ′
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi α
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi g
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi B
                        %mo +
                        %mi d
                        %mi a
                        %mo +
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi a
                        %mo ∧
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo +
                        %msub
                          %mi α
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo ∧
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        B' = \alpha_{g^{-1}}(
                        B + d a + [a \wedge a] + \alpha_*(A \wedge a)
                        )
                        \\,.
                %p The composite of two 1-morphisms
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi g
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi a
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo ′
                        %mo ,
                        %mi B
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi g
                              %mn 2
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi a
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo ″
                        %mo ,
                        %mi B
                        %mo ″
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        (A,B) \stackrel{(g_1,a_1)}{\to} (A',B') \stackrel{(g_2,a_2)}{\to}
                        (A'', B'')
                %p is given by the pair
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi g
                          %mn 1
                        %msub
                          %mi g
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mn 1
                        %mo +
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi α
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi g
                              %mn 2
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo *
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        (g_1 g_2, a_1 + (\alpha_{g_2})_* a_2)
                        \\,.
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphism"} 2-morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo :
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi g
                        %mo ,
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⇒
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi g
                        %mo ′
                        %mo ,
                        %mi a
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo :
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo ′
                        %mo ,
                        %mi B
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : (g,a) \Rightarrow (g', a'):(A,B)\to (A',B')
                  is a function
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mn ∞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        f \in C^\infty(U,G_2)
                %p such that
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo ′
                        %mo =
                        %mi δ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mi g
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        g' = \delta(f)^{-1} \cdot g
                %p and
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ′
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi Ad
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi f
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mn 1
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %mi a
                          %mo +
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msubsup
                            %mi r
                            %mi f
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                          %mo ∘
                          %msub
                            %mi α
                            %mi f
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo )
                        %mo +
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mi d
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        a' = Ad_{f^{-1}} \left(a  + (r_f^{-1} \circ \alpha_f)_*(A)\right) + f^{-1} d f
            %p
              and composition is defined as follows: vertical composition is given by pointwise multiplication (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Roberts"}> DR
              \: the order still needs sorting out!) and horizontal composition is given as horizontal composition in the one-object 2-groupoid
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G)
          %h3#ForGeneralLie2Algebras For general Lie 2-algebras
          %p
            We consider now
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            a general
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+2-algebra"} Lie 2-algebra
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}_0
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}_1
            be the two vector spaces involved and let
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msup
                    %mi b
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\{t^a\} \,, \;\;\; \{b^i\}
          %p
            be a dual basis, respectively. The structure of a Lie 2-algebra is conveniently determined by writing out the most general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi cdgAlg
                    %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  CE(\mathfrak{g}) \in cdgAlg_\mathbb{R}
          %p with these generators.
          %p We thus have
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mrow
                      %mi CE
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi a
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mi c
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi b
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi c
                  %mo −
                  %msup
                    %mi r
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %msup
                    %mi b
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d_{CE(\mathfrak{g})} t^a = - \frac{1}{2}C^a{}_{b c} t^b \wedge t^c - r^a{}_i b^i
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mrow
                      %mi CE
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mi b
                    %mi i
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msubsup
                    %mi α
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mi j
                    %mi i
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi a
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi b
                    %mi j
                  %mo −
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mi b
                      %mi c
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi a
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi b
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi c
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d_{CE(\mathfrak{g})} b^i = -\alpha^i_{a j} t^a \wedge b^j
                  \-
                  r_{a b c} t^a \wedge t^b \wedge t^c
                  \\,,
          %p
            for collections of structure constants
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{C^a{}_{b c}\}
            (the bracket on
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}_0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msubsup
                    %mi r
                    %mi a
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{r^i_a\}
            (the differential
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}_1 \to \mathfrak{g}_0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msup
                    %mi α
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\alpha^i{}_{a j}\}
            (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}_0
            on
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}_1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mi b
                      %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{r_{a b c}\}
            (the “Jacobiator” for the bracket on
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}_0
          %p
            These constants are subject to constraints (the weak
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobi+identity"} Jacobi identity
            and its higher
            = succeed "s)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherence+law"} coherence law
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mrow
                      %mi CE
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (d_{CE(\mathfrak{g})})^2 = 0
                  \\,.
          %p
            Over a test space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            a
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ←
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega^\bullet(U) \leftarrow W(\mathfrak{g})
                  \:
                  (A,B)
          %p
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weil+algebra"} Weil algebra
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(\mathfrak{g})
          %p This is given by a 1-form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A \in \Omega^1(U, \mathfrak{g}_0)
          %p and a 2-form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  B \in \Omega^2(U, \mathfrak{g}_1)
                  \\,.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
            of this is
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi β
                    %mo ,
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\beta, H)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi β
                    %mi a
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi dR
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi a
                  %mo +
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mi c
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi b
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi c
                  %mo +
                  %msup
                    %mi r
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\beta^a = d_{dR} A^a + \frac{1}{2}C^a{}_{b c} A^b \wedge A^c
                  + r^a{}_i B^i
          %p and whose 3-form component is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mi i
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi dR
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mi i
                  %mo +
                  %msup
                    %mi α
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mi j
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi a
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mi j
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi t
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mi b
                      %mi c
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi a
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi b
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi c
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H^i
                  \=
                  d_{dR} B^i
                  +
                  \\alpha^i{}_{a j} A^a \wedge B^j
                  +
                  t_{a b c} A^a \wedge A^b \wedge A^c
                  \\,.
          %h2#properties Properties
          .un_def
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong (flat Lie 2-algebra valued forms)
            %p
              The full sub-2-groupoid on
              %em flat
              Lie 2-algebra valued forms, i.e. those pairs
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,B)
              for which the 2-form
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi δ
                      %mo *
                    %mi B
                    %mo −
                    %mi d
                    %mi A
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\delta_* B - d A + [A \wedge A] = 0
            %p
              and the 3-form
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mi B
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d B + [A \wedge B] = 0
            %p
              vanishes is a resolution of the underlying discrete Lie 2-groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mo ♭
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\flat} \mathbf{B}G
              of the Lie 2-groupoid
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
          %p
            This is discussed at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+groupoid"} ∞-Lie groupoid
            in the section
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Lie+infinity-groupoid#DiffCoeffsForLie2Group"} strict Lie 2-groups – differential coefficients
          .un_def
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Π
                      %mn 2
                    %mo :
                    %mi CartSp
                    %mo →
                    %mn 2
                    %mi LieGrpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\Pi}_2 : CartSp \to 2LieGrpd
              be the smooth 2-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+groupoid"} fundamental groupoid
              functor and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mn 2
                    %mo :
                    %mi CartSp
                    %mo →
                    %mn 2
                    %mi LieGrpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_2 : CartSp \to 2LieGrpd
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+n-groupoid"} path 2-groupoid
              functor, taking values in the 2-catgeory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Difeol
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2Grpd(Difeol)
              of 2-groupoids
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+category"} internalization
              to
              = succeed "s." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+space"} diffeological space
            %ul
              %li
                %p the 2-groupoid of Lie 2-algebra valued forms for which both 2- and 3-form curvature vanish is canonically equivalent to
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Hom
                          %mrow
                            %mn 2
                            %mi Grpd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Diffeol
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi Π
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo :
                        %msup
                          %mi CartSp
                          %mi op
                        %mo →
                        %mn 2
                        %mi Grpd
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ;
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        Hom_{2Grpd(Diffeol)}(\Pi_2(-), \mathbf{B}G) : CartSp^{op} \to 2Grpd
                        \\,;
              %li
                %p the 2-groupoid of Lie 2-algebra valued forms for which the 2-form curvature vanishes is canonically equivalent to
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Hom
                          %mrow
                            %mn 2
                            %mi Grpd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Diffeol
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi P
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo :
                        %msup
                          %mi CartSp
                          %mi op
                        %mo →
                        %mn 2
                        %mi Grpd
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ;
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        Hom_{2Grpd(Diffeol)}(P_2(-), \mathbf{B}G) : CartSp^{op} \to 2Grpd
                        \\,;
          %p
            The equivalence is given by 2-dimensional
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parallel+transport"} parallel transport
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0802.0663"} SchrWalII
          %p
            The following proposition asserts that the Lie 2-groupoid of Lie 2-algebra valued forms is the coefficient object for for
            %em differential nonabelian cohomology
            in degree 2, namely for
            %em connections
            on
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+2-bundle"} principal 2-bundle
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gerbe"} gerbe
          .un_def
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (2-bundles with connection)
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+space"} paracompact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to X\}
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/good+open+cover"} good open cover
              the 2-groupoid, let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \stackrel{\simeq}{\leftarrow} C(\{U_i\})
              be the corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+nerve"} Cech nerve
              smooth 2-groupoid. Then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi Grpd
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Diffeol
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom_{2Grpd(Diffeol)}( C(\{U_i\}), \bar \mathbf{B}G)
            %p
              is equivalent to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-groupoid"} 2-groupoid
              of
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+2-bundle"} principal 2-bundle
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+2-bundle"} 2-connection
          %p
            This is discussed and proven in
            %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0802.0663"} SchrWalII
            for the case where the 2-form curvature is restricted to vanish. In this case the above can be written as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi P
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi P
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} U
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Hom( C(\{U_i\}), Hom(P_2(-), \mathbf{B}G))
                  \\simeq
                  Hom(P_2(C(\{\U_i\})), \mathbf{B}G)
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi P
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} U
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mn 2
                  %mi LieGrpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_2(C(\{\U_i\}) \in 2LieGrpd
            is a resolution of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+2-groupoid"} path 2-groupoid
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+of+Lie-algebra+valued+forms"} groupoid of Lie-algebra valued forms
            %li
              %p
                %strong 2-groupoid of Lie 2-algebra valued forms
              %ul
                %li
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+Stokes+theorem"} nonabelian Stokes theorem
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-groupoid+of+Lie+3-algebra+valued+forms"} 3-groupoid of Lie 3-algebra valued forms
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid+of+%E2%88%9E-Lie-algebra+valued+forms"} ∞-groupoid of ∞-Lie-algebra valued forms
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The 2-groupoid of Lie 2-algebra valued forms described in
            %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/PS_cache/arxiv/pdf/0802/0802.0663v3.pdf#page=27"} definition 2.11
            of
          %ul
            %li
              Schreiber, Waldorf,
              %em Smooth functors versus differential forms
              (
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+an+(%E2%88%9E%2C1)-topos+--+references#SWII"}> web
              ).
          %p
            There are many possible conventions. The one reproduced above is supposed to describe the
            %em bidual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+2-category"} opposite 2-category
            of the 2-groupoid as defined in that article, with the direction of 1- and 2-morphisms reversed.
          %p See also
          %p
            %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+an+(%E2%88%9E%2C1)-topos+--+survey#ConnectionOn2Bundle"}> differential cohomology in an (∞,1)-topos – survey - connections on 2-bundles
            \.
